  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Metformin remains the traditional first-line medication for Type 2 diabetes, but modern medical guidelines recommend SGLT2 inhibitors or GLP-1 receptor agonists as direct first-line options for patients who also have heart disease, kidney disease, or obesity .",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "modern medical guidelines recommend SGLT2 inhibitors or GLP-1 receptor agonists as direct first-line options for patients who also have heart disease, kidney disease, or obesity"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "You can read a detailed class comparison on GoodRx or explore individualized care insights via Clinical Advisor .",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "GoodRx",
            "link": "https://www.goodrx.com/conditions/diabetes-type-2/glp-1-vs-sglt2"
          },
          {
            "text": "Clinical Advisor",
            "link": "https://www.clinicaladvisor.com/features/sglt2-vs-glp-1-individualizing-diabetes-cardiovascular-and-renal-outcomes/"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "SGLT2 Inhibitors (Sodium-Glucose Cotransporter-2 Inhibitors)"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "How they work: Block glucose reabsorption in the kidneys so sugar leaves the body through urine."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Form: Daily oral pills."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "A1C reduction: Lowers blood sugar (HbA1c) by 0.5% to 1.0%."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Weight loss: Modest loss of 1 to 3 kg (2 to 7 lbs)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Best used for: Patients with heart failure or chronic kidney disease (CKD)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Common side effects: Urinary tract and genital yeast infections."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "GLP-1 Receptor Agonists (Glucagon-Like Peptide-1 Receptor Agonists)"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "How they work: Stimulate insulin release, slow stomach emptying, and signal fullness to the brain."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Form: Mostly weekly or daily injections, though oral options exist."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "A1C reduction: Lowers blood sugar by 1.0% to 1.5%."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Weight loss: Substantial loss of 4 to 6 kg (9 to 13 lbs)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Best used for: Patients needing significant weight loss or protection against atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease (ASCVD) (hardening of the arteries) and stroke."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Common side effects: Nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, and upset stomach."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "How to Choose"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Choose SGLT2 inhibitors if kidney protection or heart failure management is your top priority."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Choose GLP-1 receptor agonists if weight loss or stroke and major heart event prevention is your main goal."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, share:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Your primary health goals (weight loss, kidney/heart protection)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Any current symptoms or other health conditions"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you prepare questions to discuss with your healthcare provider."
      }
    ],
